### ariabc_pg — C++ gateway and server layer

Separate build tree at `ariabc_pg/` (CMake, see `ariabc_pg/CMakeLists.txt`).
External to PostgreSQL; communicates with it via libpq.
Two binaries are produced; Kafka support (`librdkafka`) is **required by
default** and may be made optional with `-DKAFKA_OPTIONAL=ON`.

| Path | Role |
|---|---|
| `ariabc_pg/src/ariabc_pg_server.cxx` | Main entry point for the Raft node process; parses `--id`, `--raftEndpoint`, `--clientPort`, `--raftMembers`, `--bypassRaft`, and all `db_options` / `kafka_options` flags; owns `pg_state_machine` and NuRaft lifecycle |
| `ariabc_pg/src/pg_state_machine.cxx` / `.hxx` | Implements `nuraft::state_machine`; `commit()` enqueues entries to `pg_executor`; `direct_enqueue()` / `direct_enqueue_batch()` for bypass-Raft path; tracks `last_committed_idx_` atomically |
| `ariabc_pg/src/pg_executor.cxx` / `.hxx` | Manages a libpq connection pool (`conn_pool_size=20` default); dispatches SQL to PostgreSQL; supports `exec_mode="threaded"` (N worker threads) and `exec_mode="event"` (single-thread poll reactor); owns `kafka_console_producer`; implements admission control (`queue_overloaded_`, `wait_for_admission_drain()`) and deterministic block state machine (`det_tx_state`: QUEUED→SIM_DONE→APPLY_READY→APPLIED) |
| `ariabc_pg/src/ariabc_pg_gateway.cxx` | Client-facing process; accepts connections from benchmark runners and application clients; submits to a Raft cluster via `async_cluster_submitter` or directly; handles `db_type` routing (0=safe wrapper `s <SQL>`, 1=deterministic `s <8digit_seq> <SQL>`, 2=raw SQL passthrough [default]), completion paths (`direct` or `kafka_majority`), and validation modes (`async_hash` or `strict_majority`) |
| `ariabc_pg/src/async_cluster_submitter.cxx` / `.hxx` | Shared reactor for gateway→server TCP submission; nonblocking connections with `poll()` multiplexing; self-pipe trick for wakeup; `submit_ctx` with mutex+CV for per-request synchronization |
| `ariabc_pg/src/wire_protocol.cxx` / `.hxx` | Frame-based wire protocol shared by gateway and server; `client_api_request` (req_id, sql, batch_items), `client_api_response` (status 0=OK, 1=NOT_ACCEPTED, 2=ERROR), `raft_request_batch` (leader_node_hint + items vector); `build_raft_request_log` / `parse_raft_request_log` for NuRaft log entries |
| `ariabc_pg/src/wire_protocol_async.cxx` / `.hxx` | Async (nonblocking) variants of the wire protocol used by the event-mode gateway reactor |
| `ariabc_pg/src/kafka_console.cxx` / `.hxx` | `kafka_console_producer` and `kafka_console_consumer` wrappers over librdkafka; producer profile selectable (`result_fast` or `control_durable`); consumer supports batch polling and multi-topic subscriptions |
| `ariabc_pg/src/logger.cc` / `in_memory_log_store.cxx` | NuRaft logger and in-memory Raft log store implementations |

